WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:19.169
The miller walked back from the fields to his mill.

2
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:27.338
"That little boy Nello should not spend so much time with Alois," he said to his wife that night.

3
00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:30.044
"There may be trouble later.

4
00:00:30.045 --> 00:00:35.485
He is fifteen years old, and she is twelve."

5
00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:40.695
"He is also a handsome young man," said his wife.

6
00:00:40.696 --> 00:00:43.676
"He is a good boy too."

7
00:00:43.677 --> 00:00:48.695
She looked at the portrait of Alois that Nello had drawn.

8
00:00:48.696 --> 00:00:53.905
It was hanging on the wall next to the wooden cuckoo clock.

9
00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:59.851
"Then, if they ever fell in love," said the wife, "would it matter?

10
00:00:59.852 --> 00:01:02.649
She is rich enough for both of them.

11
00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:06.846
Happiness is the most important thing!"

12
00:01:06.847 --> 00:01:09.903
"That's a foolish thing to say!"

13
00:01:09.904 --> 00:01:14.258
said the miller, slamming his pipe on the table.

14
00:01:14.259 --> 00:01:17.319
"The boy is almost a beggar.

15
00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:21.342
If he becomes a painter, he'll be worse than a beggar.

16
00:01:21.343 --> 00:01:27.684
Promise me that Nello and Alois will not play together again!"

17
00:01:27.685 --> 00:01:33.006
The miller's wife could not bear to separate them completely.

18
00:01:33.007 --> 00:01:38.032
Even so, they were kept apart in many little ways.

19
00:01:38.033 --> 00:01:43.261
After church, Nello wasn't permitted to talk with Alois.

20
00:01:43.262 --> 00:01:49.147
And in the afternoons, her parents kept her busy with chores.

21
00:01:49.148 --> 00:01:53.294
Nello was a proud and sensitive boy.

22
00:01:53.295 --> 00:01:57.610
He realized what was happening and was hurt.

23
00:01:57.611 --> 00:02:04.326
So, Nello and Patrasche no longer went to the mill to visit Alois.

24
00:02:04.327 --> 00:02:09.486
"Why can't I see my friend Alois?" Nello thought.

25
00:02:09.487 --> 00:02:12.776
"I haven't done anything wrong!"

26
00:02:12.777 --> 00:02:17.808
He wondered if he had angered the miller that day in the fields.

27
00:02:17.809 --> 00:02:22.971
He did not know that his only sin was being poor.

28
00:02:22.972 --> 00:02:28.046
Sometimes, Nello and Alois ran into each other.

29
00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:33.447
When that happened, he held her hand and told her to go home.

30
00:02:33.448 --> 00:02:38.073
"Sorry, Alois, but your father will be angry.

31
00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:41.296
He thinks that I make you idle.

32
00:02:41.297 --> 00:02:43.809
You must go."

33
00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:47.678
Nello said this with a sad heart.

34
00:02:47.679 --> 00:02:53.242
Without Alois, the earth did not look as bright as it used to.

35
00:02:53.243 --> 00:02:56.488
But Nello did not complain.

36
00:02:56.489 --> 00:03:03.435
As his grandfather said, "We are poor and must take what God sends.

37
00:03:03.436 --> 00:03:06.882
The poor cannot choose."

38
00:03:06.883 --> 00:03:12.729
One day, little Alois found Nello walking near the canal.

39
00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:16.183
She ran up to him, crying.

40
00:03:16.184 --> 00:03:22.745
Tomorrow was her birthday, but she was not allowed to invite him to her party.

41
00:03:22.746 --> 00:03:28.754
In other years, Nello had always been at her birthday party.

42
00:03:28.755 --> 00:03:33.748
Nello kissed her on the cheek and asked her to stop crying.

43
00:03:33.749 --> 00:03:38.537
He told her, "It will be different one day, Alois.

44
00:03:38.538 --> 00:03:45.337
One day, that little portrait your father has will be worth a lot of money.

45
00:03:45.338 --> 00:03:50.238
Then your father will invite me in again," Nello said.

46
00:03:50.239 --> 00:03:54.357
"Just remember me always, dear little Alois.

47
00:03:54.358 --> 00:04:00.636
If you do, I promise that, one day, I will be a great artist."

48
00:04:00.637 --> 00:04:02.949
"And if I forget you?"

49
00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:07.416
the pretty child asked, pouting a little.

50
00:04:07.417 --> 00:04:13.148
Nello's eyes left her face and wandered to the distant horizon.

51
00:04:13.149 --> 00:04:18.719
There was a smile on his face both sweet and sad.

52
00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:23.354
"I will be great still," he said under his breath.

53
00:04:23.355 --> 00:04:27.644
"I will be great still, or die, Alois."

54
00:04:27.645 --> 00:04:33.518
The next evening, Nello sat at the door of the hut with Patrasche.

55
00:04:33.519 --> 00:04:38.311
He heard the sounds of Alois' birthday celebrations.

56
00:04:38.312 --> 00:04:44.731
"Never mind, Patrasche," he said, with his arms around the dog's neck.

57
00:04:44.732 --> 00:04:51.646
"It will all be different one day."
